Bridge webhook (webhooks.py):
  - HMAC-SHA256 signature verification (X-Bridge-Signature header)
  - DB lookup of payout task via finogrid_task_id in transfer metadata
  - Append ExecutionEvent (PARTNER_STATUS_UPDATE / PARTNER_COMPLETED /
    PARTNER_FAILED / TASK_CANCELLED) based on Bridge transfer status
  - Update task.status and task.partner_tx_id; set failure_reason on fail
  - Publish reconciliation-trigger Pub/Sub message on every callback

KYT webhook (webhooks.py):
  - HMAC-SHA256 signature verification (X-Kyt-Signature header)
  - Persist raw compliance payload to task.compliance_result
  - Map decision (approved/pass → EXECUTING, rejected/fail → FAILED,
    review/unknown → HELD_FOR_REVIEW) + append COMPLIANCE_PASS /
    COMPLIANCE_FAIL / COMPLIANCE_HOLD ExecutionEvent

bridge_client.py:
  - Replace hardcoded "ethereum" with get_adapter(corridor_code)
    .get_chain_for_asset(asset) — Nigeria uses Tron for USDT,
    Vietnam uses Tron for USDT, others default to ethereum

KYA validator — Sardine polling (mcp/kya_validator/server.py):
  - get_kya_status now fetches GET /kyc/sessions/{sardine_session_id}
  - Maps Sardine approved → mint token (enhanced if riskScore < 30,
    else basic); rejected → status=rejected; pending → no-op
  - Graceful error handling — poll failures log warnings, don't 500

config.py: add bridge_webhook_secret + kyt_webhook_secret settings

